    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d104">

                <pb facs="0171" n="95" sameAs="frus:frus1916/pg95"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 893.00/2543</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Consul Peck to the
                            Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 113</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Consulate</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Tsingtau</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1916-09-26">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">September 26, 1916</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to state that according
                    to local reports the so-called revolutionist troops at Weihsien and Choutsun
                    have arrived at some sort of an understanding with the Central Government and
                    have submitted to it. This despatch has been delayed some days in the effort to
                    learn the details of the agreement, but even persons who have been to those
                    cities have been able to do little but confirm the report of the surrender. A
                    gradual disbanding is going on and part of the forces will be incorporated with
                    the Chinese Army.</p>
                <p>It is reported that many of the brigands and other recruits from Manchuria are
                    being returned thither. The volunteer constabulary organized around Weihsien to
                    protect the residents from the revolutionary troops are also being disbanded and
                    more peaceful conditions are being established.</p>
                <p>A copy of this despatch has been sent to the Legation at Peking and to the
                    Consulate at Chefoo.</p>
                <p>I have [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Willys R. Peck</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
